  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe DXF reader now imports an AutoCAD 2000 (AC1015) export with a `CLASSES` section.\n\n- The reader skips the `CLASSES`, `THUMBNAILIMAGE` and `ACDSDATA` sections to their `ENDSEC`. These sections hold no geometry. A missing `ENDSEC` is a named error. Each other unknown section stays refused.\n- The `OBJECTS` reader reads a balanced group 102 bracket (`102 {ACAD_REACTORS` .. `102 }`) as opaque data. An unclosed, nested, unopened or malformed bracket is a named error.\n- A `DICTIONARY` keeps all its checks from #3176.\n- Each other object (for example `LAYOUT`, `ACDBDICTIONARYWDFLT`, `ACDBPLACEHOLDER`) is an inert record. The reader takes only its handle and its owner. The object must join the ownership graph of #3176. An unowned object, a duplicate handle and an object count over the limit are refused.\n- Second review (new in this push): a record with an entity name (`LINE`, `LWPOLYLINE`, `INSERT` and so on) in `OBJECTS`, `CLASSES`, `THUMBNAILIMAGE` or `ACDSDATA` is refused. Before this change, such a record without the `AcDbEntity` marker was dropped with no diagnostic. The list is `ENTITY_KINDS` in `crates/geometry/src/dxf/entities.rs`.\n\nThis change loosens a refusal that #3176 added on purpose. `docs/decisions/3450-dxf-classes-section.md` says how the #3176 law changed. Rule 1 (no section that can hold geometry is skipped) and rule 2 (no record is accepted by its name) stay. Rule 3 (each object type has its own checks) is replaced, for objects other than `DICTIONARY`, by one general rule: the reader takes no value from an inert object, and an object is drawn only through an entity in `ENTITIES` or `BLOCKS`, which stay strict.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe three QA files of the issue were read through `dxf::parse` and `SketchData::from_dxf` on this branch, with a temporary local test. The files are not committed, because they are not ours to commit.\n\n| File | Primitives | Closed chains | Open | Rejected |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `q04-vcarve-sign-letters.dxf` (AC1015) | 300 | 2 (261.70 mm² each) | 0 | 0 |\n| `q04-vcarve-sign-letters-r12.dxf` | 894 | 2 (261.79 mm² each) | 0 | 0 |\n| `q06-die-lines.dxf` (AC1015) | 117 | 1 (617.34 mm²) | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe R12 twin gives line segments for the arcs, so its area is 0.04 % larger.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/geometry/tests/dxf_ac1015_fixture.rs` (new, hand-written fixture with the section and object layout of the real export):\n  - `an_ac1015_export_gives_the_same_closed_chains_as_its_r12_twin`\n  - `a_truncated_ac1015_export_never_imports`\n  - `a_mutated_ac1015_export_never_panics`\n  - `many_inert_objects_stop_at_the_entity_limit`\n- `crates/geometry/tests/dxf_classes_section.rs` (8): for example `classes_section_is_skipped_and_entities_import`, `classes_section_without_endsec_is_a_named_error`, `other_unknown_sections_stay_refused`, `an_entity_in_a_section_without_geometry_is_refused`.\n- `crates/geometry/tests/dxf_objects_section.rs` (5): `ac1015_classes_and_objects_import_the_same_entities_as_the_bare_file`, `unbalanced_group_102_blocks_are_named_errors`, `a_file_that_ends_inside_objects_is_a_named_error`, `inert_objects_must_be_owned_members_of_the_object_tree`, `object_data_after_the_subclass_marker_stays_opaque`.\n- The #3176 pins in `dxf_inert_sections.rs` (4) pass with no change.\n\n## Gates (head `8f3c42407`, main merged in, `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 1149 steps, 1148 ok, 1 failed. The failed step is `clippy -D warnings`: `clippy::needless_range_loop` in `crates/gpu/src/cut.rs:126`. This PR does not change `crates/gpu`. The lint comes from the local toolchain (clippy for Rust 1.99) on code of main.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- DXF and importer suites in the quick gate: geometry `dxf` 17, `dxf_ac1015_fixture` 4, `dxf_classes_section` 8, `dxf_inert_sections` 4, `dxf_objects_section` 5, `dxf_profile` 5, `dxf_refusals` 15, `dxf_writer` 3, `sketch_data` 9; app `contour_dxf_sketch` 4, `contour_dxf_sketch_mixed` 2, `contour_dxf_sketch_verify` 3, `contour_dxf_profiles` 1, `slot_dxf_sketch` 5, `mcp_dxf` 2, `tool_dxf_profile` 6, `tool_dxf_profile_mcp` 1, `wire_dxf_selection` 3; tools `tool_dxf_profile` 4; ui `contour_dxf_sketch` 2. All pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate light` on `8f3c42407`: 3 steps, 0 failed (`light build`, `motion light: lib`, `motion light: adaptive_troch_parallel`).\n- Full heavy lanes: not run (rule #3556).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real QA files are not in the repository. Only the hand-written fixture pins them.\n- An extension dictionary owned by an entity or a table record still fails the owner check (`unresolved dictionary owner`), as before.\n- No import through the GUI or MCP with the real files on this head.\n\nChangelog: DXF import reads AutoCAD 2000 (AC1015) files with CLASSES, THUMBNAILIMAGE, ACDSDATA sections and layout objects, and refuses an entity record in a section that holds no geometry.\n\nFixes #3450\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
